# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5.memetic-wikitext" "A named value rides in ticks, and a lar: address inside one stops at the closing tick"

# EVERY VALUE OF A CALL RIDES NAMED AND TICKED (the kupono grammar). TiddlyWiki reads `name=`value``
# as a substituted attribute value, and the dialect adds nothing on top of it: the key is an
# attribute name, the ticks are the substituted value's own punctuation, and the text between them
# is the value.

<<~ persona name=`Lares` params=`a multitude`>>
#           ^^^^ entity.other.attribute-name.argument.tiddlywiki5
#               ^ keyword.operator.assignment.tiddlywiki5
#                ^ punctuation.definition.substituted.single.attribute.begin.tiddlywiki5
#                 ^^^^^ string.template.substituted.single.attribute.html.tiddlywiki5
#                      ^ punctuation.definition.substituted.single.attribute.end.tiddlywiki5
#                        ^^^^^^ entity.other.attribute-name.argument.tiddlywiki5

# A LAR: ADDRESS STOPS AT THE CLOSING TICK. The `from=` end of a call is a lar: URI inside ticks. Its
# region used to run to whitespace, a quote or a bracket, so the closing tick fell INSIDE the address
# and the rest of the call read as value text: `to=` was no attribute, and the call's own `>>`
# never closed. A backtick now ends the address, so the next key reads as the key it is.

<<~ set lares=`aim` from=`lar:///a.b.c/x` to=`?` mode=`draft`>>
#                                      ^ variable.other.constant.path.lar.memetic-wikitext
#                                       ^ punctuation.definition.substituted.single.attribute.end.tiddlywiki5
#                                         ^^ entity.other.attribute-name.argument.tiddlywiki5
#                                                ^^^^ entity.other.attribute-name.argument.tiddlywiki5

# The same holds for BOTH ends of a pranala, and the address wears its colourless parent, never the string's.

<<~ pranala from=`lar:///a.b.c/x` to=`lar:///a.b.c/y`>>
#                                 ^^ entity.other.attribute-name.argument.tiddlywiki5
#                                                  ^ variable.other.constant.path.lar.memetic-wikitext

# A SLOT WORD RIDES AS `slot=`: the fragment inside the ticks reads as the anchor it names.

<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>
#       ^^^^ entity.other.attribute-name.argument.tiddlywiki5
#             ^ punctuation.definition.anchor.memetic-wikitext
